                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Just like the first game , Dragon's Lair II has very little in terms of gameplay. This is simply a QTE fest where you need to press the right button at the right time to progress in the story. Pretty cool for the 80's ... not so much for modern standards. \nBut this game manages to be utterly worse than the original !\nFirst , if you make a wrong move you will have to restart the full level. That didn't happened in the original game. \nSecond , there are hidden treasures in the levels ... and you can't finish the game if you don't find them all. Yeah , you will be actually locked out from the last level and be forced to play trough the whole game again until you find all the treasures. \nThird the art direction is all over the place. In the first game you were trying to save a princess from an evil wizard's castle , finding what you you're suposed to in such a fantasy setting. In this game you'll be \"time travelling\" trough ancient Egypt , meeting Beethoven , Adam and Eve in Paradise and Alice in Wonderland. Yeah the game makes absolutely no sense. \nAt least you can watch the whole game as a movie ( there's an option to do so ).",
